SQL>   -- The demo application (planning/spec-patch-08-road-kit-demo-app.md, in road-cal).
SQL>   --
SQL>   -- This package exists to be READ, and to fail loudly when the framework breaks. It is the
SQL>   -- smallest application that pulls on every seam an adopter will pull on: permission-gated
SQL>   -- handlers, an application role, a RESERVED application permission, per-principal ownership, and
SQL>   -- optimistic concurrency through road_audit_api.
SQL>   --
SQL>   -- It is not a product and not a starter template. Nobody should build on top of it.
SQL>   --
SQL>   -- Rule 1 of the patch, which keeps it honest: THE DEMO APP MAY NEVER CAUSE A FRAMEWORK CHANGE.
SQL>   -- If it needs something road-kit lacks, that is a specification question for the framework,
SQL>   -- raised separately -- never a change smuggled in under a demo.
SQL>   --
SQL>   -- Signature convention matches road_admin_api and road-cal's event_api: native JSON in, native
SQL>   -- JSON out, no ref cursors or PL/SQL collections across the package boundary. Never commits --
SQL>   -- ORDS commits on success and tests roll back to a savepoint.
SQL>   --
SQL>   -- Authorisation is enforced HERE, not only in the handler, for the same reason road_admin_api
SQL>   -- does it: a second caller -- an MCP tool, a batch job, another package -- must not reach a
SQL>   -- privileged operation by not being an ORDS handler.
SQL> 
